# Legal documents — sync, acceptance bump, lawyer package

## 1. Sync App ↔ Web (same change)

When editing published legal content, review **all** related surfaces in the same task:

| Document | Canonical / locations |
|----------|------------------------|
| Privacy | Web `privacy.html` + `en/privacy.html` (app links to web; EN app terms should link to `/en/privacy.html`) |
| Terms (web) | `terms.html` + `en/terms.html` |
| Cookies | `cookies.html` + `en/cookies.html` |
| Terms (app) | `TourAI.App/Resources/Terms/Terms.es-ES.html` + `Terms.en-GB.html` |
| Flows | `delete-account.html`, `reset-password.html` (+ `en/` mirrors) if wording changes |

Do not leave App Terms and Web Privacy/Terms out of sync for the same policy change.

**Web copy:** user-facing legal text lives in **HTML**, not in `js/locales/*.js`.

## 2. Acceptance version (mandatory)

Follow **`legal-acceptance-version.mdc`**: bump `PublicConfig/Legal.CurrentVersion` and all fallbacks to **today’s** `YYYY-MM-DD`.

## 3. Lawyer package (outside Git)

Lawyer tooling: `D:\Proyectos\Documents\legal-export`

- **Sources:** Spanish web legal pages (`privacy.html`, `terms.html`, `cookies.html`, …), app `Terms.*.html`, `lawyer-review-notes.html`.
- **Regenerate PDFs/ZIP:** `node D:\Proyectos\Documents\legal-export\scripts\build-lawyer-package.js`
- **Before the first lawyer send:** maintain a single current corpus (no `reviews/` delta folders required).
- **After a lawyer has reviewed a package:** for the next change set, create immutable `legal-export/reviews/yyyyMMdd - ShortTitle/` with `SCOPE.md`, `DIFF-NOTES.md`, `outgoing/`, `lawyer-response/` (see historical rule in TourAI repo if needed).

Do not copy `legal-export` into the web or app Git repos.

## 4. Reply to the owner

State: acceptance version bumped (or not), App/Web sync done, and whether Firestore `PublicConfig/Legal` still needs a manual update.
